<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan MFIG group to tender for 56-60,000T US corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan MFIG group to tender for 56-60,000T US corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Members Feed Industry Group will tender on Wednesday for 56,000 to 60,000 tonnes of U.S. No.2 corn, traders said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The feed group's main buyers are Taiwan's Formosa Oilseed, Fomau Cereal, Morn Sun Feed Mill and Shin Tai Industry.</p>
<p>Traders said the suppliers have an option to offer the shipment between 56,000 and 60,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Details of the shipment are as follows:</p>
<p> Shipment   Tonnage Date/Location</p>
<p>		U.S. Gulf    Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> 56-60,000  Oct 7-21     Oct 22-Nov 5</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
<p>-- Internet  taipei.newsroom@reuters.com</p>
